{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json\\\"; d=json.load(open(p)); print(type(d).__name__); print(str(d)[:2500])' \"","aggregated_output":"list\n[{'number': 1, 'title': 'Will there be a license?', 'created_at': '2020-01-23T19:34:37Z', 'closed_at': '2020-01-26T15:31:06Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': \"First off, _AWESOME_ project. I'll definitely be tinkering with this.\\r\\n\\r\\nQuestion: will you be applying a license to the code? I'm not here to push any license, but I do think at least _having_ a license is a good idea.\\r\\n\\r\\nGood job on the project 👏 👏 \"}, {'number': 2, 'title': 'Great lib!  Trouble with width', 'created_at': '2020-01-26T03:01:29Z', 'closed_at': '2020-03-09T11:50:01Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': \"I'm really liking this library!  \\r\\n\\r\\nOne thing ... I seem to be having trouble with tables with widths greater than 80 chars.  Tried the various width options, but no luck.  Thoughts?\\r\\n\\r\\nThanks.\"}, {'number': 3, 'title': 'Markdown tables', 'created_at': '2020-01-26T16:28:59Z', 'closed_at': '2020-05-28T13:58:04Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': \"Hi @willmcgugan! Looks like an awesome library. I'm really interested in using this for terminal rendering of Markdown files, but I need to be able to render Markdown tables. Is that something you think would fit in this library?\"}, {'number': 4, 'title': 'Document whether Windows is supported', 'created_at': '2020-01-26T19:07:41Z', 'closed_at': '2020-01-27T16:23:38Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': \"I can't tell from the documentation, or the PyPI classifiers, whether Windows is supported. I'd like it if it were, but obviously that's up to you as a developer. But could you document more clearly whether you do, so that I don't have to download the library and try it out to check?\"}, {'number': 6, 'title': 'README.md - table.add_column error in readme', 'created_at': '2020-01-29T12:53:38Z', 'closed_at': '2020-01-29T13:36:41Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': 'In readme there is a row that is wrong in the add_column.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom:\\r\\ntable.add_columngit (\"Production Budget\", justify=\"right\")\\r\\n\\r\\nTo:\\r\\ntable.add_column (\"Production Budget\", justify=\"right\")\\r\\n'}, {'number': 7, 'title': 'Console width off by one on some terminals / ssh', 'created_at': '2020-02-04T10:07:43Z', 'closed_at': '2020-02-04T18:32:13Z', 'state_reason': 'completed', 'body': 'On some consoles the output width seems to be calculated one character too wide. See the following example:\\r\\n```\\r\\n>>> from rich.console import Console\\r\\n>>> from rich.table import Table\\r\\n>>> c = Console()\\r\\n>>> t = Table(\"Yo!\", \"Tables!\")\\r\\n>>> t.add_r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
